  "description": "A large open medical and life-science AI agent skill library for the OpenClaw / NanoClaw framework — ~869 SKILL.md modules across clinical, genomics, drug-discovery, bioinformatics, omics, and data-science categories. The clinical set (~119 skills) covers areas such as clinical reports, decision support, prior authorisation, FHIR development, and HIPAA compliance; the majority is research/bioinformatics tooling (variant calling, single-cell, genomics databases). MIT-licensed; skills are read directly by a model-agnostic agent and require a user-supplied LLM/API key. The clinical skills are not described as independently validated, and this is agent tooling, not a cleared medical device.",
